  "query_preview": "..Moisture continues to stream into Arizona, as deep \nand layered southwest flow persists over the southwest United \nStates. The bulk of the moisture resides in New Mexico, but outflows \nare pushing higher dew points into portions of eastern, southern and \ncentral Arizona this afternoon.\n\nThe 18Z KFGZ sounding indicates relatively low instability and some \ndry air in the mid-levels, so storms that do develop today probably \nwill not have much of a bite. \n\nMore of the same Thursday and Friday, maybe a bit more in the way of \ndynamics as a trough axis approaches from the NW. Drier weather is \nlikely to develop behind this trough axis for Saturday and maybe \nSunday.\n\nThen, all eyes on the sub-tropics as we wait and see of one of these \nhurricanes will induce a surge or provide some mid-level moistening. \nIt is a little early to make that call at this time, but the door is \ndefinitely open for it to happen. Stay tuned.",
